  "asr": {
    "pitch_10_sanjay.mp4": {
      "wer": 0.091,
      "transcript": "Hi everyone, I'm Sanjay from Team Obit, and here is our pitch for Voltride. Our recommendation is to stay in Pune for the next 18 months and build a dense battery swapping network before chasing new cities. Right now each scooter spends almost 40 minutes a day of the road waiting for a van to collect and recharge it. And that idle time is the biggest reason the fleet unsolittle. 20 swap stations near the busiest pickup zones would lift utilization from 5.1 to 6.4 rides per scooter per day. Thank you for listening."
    },
    "pitch_11_leela.mp4": {
      "wer": 0.123,
      "transcript": "Hello judges, this is Leela from Team Northstar. We believe Volt Ride should launch in Coimbart or with women commuters as the first customer segment. Our interviews showed that many women avoid crowded buses in the evening, and a scooter with a panic button and live trip sharing would feel safer. We would start with 150 scooters near the women's colleges. Thank you."
    }
  },
